    "narrative": "The LawDog core is primed for production tonight, led by **Jonathan Aranda**, our strongest play with a 68.94 score. Batting second against Kolek, **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a potent mix of wind blowing out, a favorable SP xERA of 4.36, and a significant dynamic platoon advantage. While **Bryson Stott** (63.08) and **Masyn Winn** (62.77) also clear the 60-point threshold for strong starts, they face different dynamics; **Masyn Winn** is the primary beneficiary of the day\u2019s most exploitable matchup against the 7.82 xERA of Waldrep, while **Bryson Stott** maintains a solid floor despite a slight downgrade due to the opposing catcher's elite 1.86s pop time, which threatens his stolen base potential in our scarcity-focused build.\n\n**Cal Raleigh** (56.58) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.95) occupy the marginal tier, rounding out the starting lineup. **Gavin Sheets** gets a nice boost from hitting in the cleanup spot, though the matchup against Sasaki remains a test of his efficiency. **Cal Raleigh** sits just shy of the strong start threshold, primarily dragged down by park factors and a negative platoon split against Ure\u00f1a. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining sidelined on the IL, our depth is tested today; **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert** all missed the cut, primarily due to the team off-day constraints affecting the middle and bottom of our roster. Keep a close watch on **Cal Raleigh**\u2019s final order position, as any move down the lineup could further depress his efficiency against Ure\u00f1a.",
